r crew cooperation despite communication difficulty. Or we could argue that Candidate B's stress resilience and conscientiousness make him a strong alternative.\n\nWe need to make a focused argument. Perhaps we can challenge D's suitability by highlighting the moody/loner aspects, and propose Candidate B as a better balanced candidate, given his stress resilience, conscientiousness, and technical skills, while his communication tone issues may be less severe than D's moody loner behavior.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 1 and Agent 2 recommended D. We can say \"I understand the support for D, but I have concerns about his moody and loner traits, which could impair crew cooperation, especially on long-haul flights where teamwork is critical. In contrast, Candidate B demonstrates strong reliability (very conscientious), excellent stress handling, and good technical competence, and while he sometimes adopts the wrong tone, this may be more manageable.\"\n\nWe need to use explicit facts: D is considered moody, regarded as a loner. B is very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also B sometimes adopts wrong tone. Provide implication.\n\nThus we can shift vote to Candidate B. Or we could keep D but ask for more info. The process says we should aim to converge. We can propose a change.\n\nLet's decide to shift to Candidate B, providing reasoning.\n\nWe also might ask a question to Agent 1 about D's reliability evidence, but we can still give a vote now. The instruction: If a relevant criterion is unclear, first check your own notes. If not, ask a specific question before writing public message. We have a concern about D's reliability evidence; we don't have any. But we can still make an argument based on known concerns. It's okay.\n\nThus we will produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I understand the support for D, but I have concerns about his moody and loner traits, which could impair crew cooperation. Candidate B, on the other hand, shows strong reliability (very conscientious), stress resilience, technical competence, and while he sometimes adopts the wrong tone, that seems less detrimental than D's interpersonal issues. Therefore I shift my vote to Candidate B.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: D considered moody, regarded as a loner; B very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, sometimes adopts wrong tone.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
